                    {"q": "What's the difference between Photo AI, Gigapixel AI, and Video AI?", "a": "Photo AI focuses on general repair (noise, blur, exposure), Gigapixel AI specializes in upscaling resolution, and Video AI applies similar fixes plus frame interpolation to video."},
                    {"q": "What are Astra and Bloom for?", "a": "They're cloud tools aimed specifically at cleaning up AI-generated video (Astra) and AI-generated images (Bloom), restoring realistic detail that diffusion and generative video models often smooth away."},
                    {"q": "Can I use Topaz as a plugin inside other software?", "a": "Yes, the desktop apps integrate as plugins with Lightroom, Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, and other NLEs/DAMs."},
                    {"q": "Is there a free trial?", "a": "Topaz offers free trials of its apps with watermarked or resolution-limited exports so you can test quality before subscribing."},
                    {"q": "Does Topaz require a powerful computer?", "a": "Local rendering is GPU-intensive; Topaz recommends a dedicated GPU for smooth performance, especially in Video AI, and performance can lag on older or integrated-graphics machines."}
