                    {"title": "FireAttention kernels", "desc": "A proprietary CUDA kernel that Fireworks says delivers meaningfully faster inference than standard serving stacks, reducing both latency and cost per request."},
                    {"title": "On-demand GPU deployments", "desc": "Dedicated H100, H200, B200, B300, and GB300 GPU instances billed per GPU-second, for teams that need guaranteed capacity and higher rate limits than serverless."},
                    {"title": "LoRA fine-tuning", "desc": "Cost-efficient LoRA-based fine-tuning that enables instant deployment and rapid switching between up to 100 fine-tuned model adapters without redeploying infrastructure."},
                    {"title": "FireFunction", "desc": "A dedicated function-calling model that helps developers build compound AI systems combining multiple models, modalities (text, audio, image), and external APIs."},
                    {"title": "Multiple serving tiers", "desc": "Standard, Priority, and Fast serving tiers let teams trade off cost against latency guarantees depending on workload requirements."},
                    {"title": "Disaggregated serving and speculative decoding", "desc": "Architectural optimizations that improve throughput and support longer context lengths than conventional serving approaches."},
                    {"title": "Broad model catalog", "desc": "Supports major open-weight model families including Llama, DeepSeek, Qwen, Mixtral, GLM, and Kimi, with new releases added quickly after launch."}
